{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9vrTyPmXpB2SpJ1rRDk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A handler that panics with `http.ErrAbortHandler` is now handled the same way as a broken pipe. The recovery middleware logs a one-line message without a stack trace, records the error, aborts, and doesn't write a 500.\n\n- **Change:** `recovery.go` now treats any panic value where `errors.Is(err, http.ErrAbortHandler)` is true as a broken connection. `net/http` deliberately skips logging for this sentinel, so dumping a full stack trace for it was just noise.\n- **Test:** I added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` in `recovery_test.go`. It checks that the status code the handler already set is kept, that the error text is logged, and that no \"panic recovered\" stack dump appears. The gate passed: the test fails without the fix and passes with it.\n- **One behaviour change:** a custom handler passed to `CustomRecovery` is no longer called for this panic, the same as for broken pipes.\n- **Not run:** I didn't run the full test suite or the linter, only the `TestPanic*` tests."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1141,"cache_read_input_tokens":33896,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1141,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6892aa37-140e-4aa3-93fc-984328009eec","uuid":"b8eac447-f7f1-47e7-aec5-185a06a8e584","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:20:55.097Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9vrTkjcgaGxQGcu47tV"}
